# Praxis lint warning budget — the ratchet contract.
#
# `bun run lint` (scripts/lint-with-budget.mjs) runs eslint with
# --max-warnings set to the number on the last non-comment line of this
# file. The contract:
#
#   - Errors ALWAYS fail the build, budget or no budget.
#   - Warnings fail the build only when the total count EXCEEDS this
#     budget — which means zero NEW warnings are allowed, ever.
#   - The budget may only move DOWN: fix some warnings, verify
#     `bun run lint:raw` reports the new lower count, then lower the
#     number here to match. Raising it requires explicit justification
#     in the change that touches this file.
#
# Why a budget instead of "fix all 368 now": the debt is concentrated
# in categories where mechanical fixes are genuinely risky —
#   159 x @typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars  (case-by-case judgment)
#    88 x react-hooks/exhaustive-deps        (rewriting hook dependency
#                                             arrays changes effect
#                                             re-execution semantics —
#                                             a dedicated refactor)
#    49 x no-mixed-spaces-and-tabs           (mostly inside template
#                                             literals holding embedded
#                                             Python source, where the
#                                             whitespace IS the program)
#    25 x no-useless-escape, 13 x prefer-const, plus assorted small counts.
# Blindly "fixing" these in one pass is exactly the kind of sweep that
# causes the layout and save-semantics regressions this pipeline exists
# to prevent. The ratchet lets the debt shrink safely over time.
#
# Baseline recorded 2026-11-21: 368 warnings, 0 errors.
# 2026-11-21 (Phase 2): lowered to 367 — the split-engine / tab-lifecycle
# extraction removed one legacy unused-var warning outright.
# 2026-11-21 (Phase 2b): lowered to 360 — the code-viewer decomposition
# moved seven more warning-carrying lines into extracted modules (and
# pruned 82 imports the extraction orphaned).
# 2026-11-21 (Phase 3, Pyright LSP): lowered to 358 — the integration
# itself landed warning-neutral after cleanups: the hover-tooltip memo's
# deps went complete (dropping one stale eslint-disable directive) and
# the two view-mode mouse/click handlers list `lines` outright instead
# of the lines.length shorthand their new LSP branches invalidate.
358
